      "startFrame": 0,
      "durationInFrames": 32,
      "stateImagePublicPath": "narration/generated/states/s001-c000.png"
    },
    {
      "id": "promise-call-here",
      "index": 1,
      "page": 1,
      "click": 1,
      "text": "The call happens in the current runtime, but the implementation can live in a Worker, a child process, a desktop host, or even the far end of a message queue.",
      "audioPublicPath": "narration/audio/s001-c001.mp3",
      "audioDurationMs": 500,
      "silentMs": 0,
      "transitionMs": 300,
      "leadInMs": 100,
      "tailMs": 150,
      "transitionFrames": 9,
      "leadInFrames": 3,
      "audioFrames": 15,
      "tailFrames": 5,
      "startFrame": 32,
      "durationInFrames": 32,
      "stateImagePublicPath": "narration/generated/states/s001-c001.png"
    },
    {
      "id": "promise-result",
      "index": 2,
      "page": 1,
      "click": 2,
      "text": "To the application code, the result is still just a Promise.",
      "audioPublicPath": "narration/audio/s001-c002.mp3",
      "audioDurationMs": 500,
      "silentMs": 0,
      "transitionMs": 300,
      "leadInMs": 100,
      "tailMs": 150,
      "transitionFrames": 9,
      "leadInFrames": 3,
      "audioFrames": 15,
      "tailFrames": 5,
      "startFrame": 64,
      "durationInFrames": 32,
      "stateImagePublicPath": "narration/generated/states/s001-c002.png"
    },
    {
      "id": "promise-mental-model",
      "index": 3,
      "page": 1,
      "click": 3,
      "text": "kkRPC's whole goal is to compress cross-boundary communication down to exactly this mental model.",
      "audioPublicPath": "narration/audio/s001-c003.mp3",
      "audioDurationMs": 500,
      "silentMs": 0,
      "transitionMs": 300,
      "leadInMs": 100,
      "tailMs": 150,
      "transitionFrames": 9,
      "leadInFrames": 3,
      "audioFrames": 15,
      "tailFrames": 5,
      "startFrame": 96,
      "durationInFrames": 32,
      "stateImagePublicPath": "narration/generated/states/s001-c003.png"
    },
    {
      "id": "jsonrpc-wire-format",
      "index": 4,
      "page": 2,
      "click": 0,
      "text": "JSON-RPC is good at defining what goes on the wire.",
      "audioPublicPath": "narration/audio/s002-c000.mp3",
      "audioDurationMs": 500,
      "silentMs": 0,
      "transitionMs": 300,
      "leadInMs": 100,
      "tailMs": 150,
      "transitionFrames": 9,
      "leadInFrames": 3,
      "audioFrames": 15,
      "tailFrames": 5,
      "startFrame": 128,
      "durationInFrames": 32,
      "stateImagePublicPath": "narration/generated/states/s002-c000.png"
    },
    {
      "id": "jsonrpc-version",
      "index": 5,
      "page": 2,
      "click": 1,
      "text": "It gives the request a version.",
      "audioPublicPath": "narration/audio/s002-c001.mp3",
      "audioDurationMs": 500,
      "silentMs": 0,
      "transitionMs": 300,
      "leadInMs": 100,
      "tailMs": 150,
      "transitionFrames": 9,
      "leadInFrames": 3,
      "audioFrames": 15,
      "tailFrames": 5,
      "startFrame": 160,
      "durationInFrames": 32,
      "stateImagePublicPath": "narration/generated/states/s002-c001.png"
    },
    {
      "id": "jsonrpc-method",
      "index": 6,
      "page": 2,
      "click": 2,
      "text": "It names the method to call.",
      "audioPublicPath": "narration/audio/s002-c002.mp3",
      "audioDurationMs": 500,
      "silentMs": 0,
      "transitionMs": 300,
      "leadInMs": 100,
      "tailMs": 150,
      "transitionFrames": 9,
      "leadInFrames": 3,
      "audioFrames": 15,
      "tailFrames": 5,
      "startFrame": 192,
      "durationInFrames": 32,
      "stateImagePublicPath": "narration/generated/states/s002-c002.png"
    },
    {
      "id": "jsonrpc-params",
      "index": 7,
      "page": 2,
      "click": 3,
      "text": "It carries the parameters for that method.",
      "audioPublicPath": "narration/audio/s002-c003.mp3",
      "audioDurationMs": 500,
      "silentMs": 0,
      "transitionMs": 300,
      "leadInMs": 100,
      "tailMs": 150,
      "transitionFrames": 9,
      "leadInFrames": 3,
      "audioFrames": 15,
      "tailFrames": 5,
      "startFrame": 224,
      "durationInFrames": 32,
      "stateImagePublicPath": "narration/generated/states/s002-c003.png"
    },
    {
      "id": "jsonrpc-id",
      "index": 8,
      "page": 2,
      "click": 4,
      "text": "And it supplies an id for correlating the request and response. That part is fine.",
      "audioPublicPath": "narration/audio/s002-c004.mp3",
      "audioDurationMs": 500,
      "silentMs": 0,
      "transitionMs": 300,
      "leadInMs": 100,
      "tailMs": 150,
      "transitionFrames": 9,
      "leadInFrames": 3,
      "audioFrames": 15,
      "tailFrames": 5,
      "startFrame": 256,
      "durationInFrames": 32,
      "stateImagePublicPath": "narration/generated/states/s002-c004.png"
    },
    {
      "id": "jsonrpc-protocol-leak",
      "index": 9,
      "page": 2,
      "click": 5,
      "text": "But when application code assembles these objects by hand, serialization, request correlation, and dispatch logic leak into every call site.",
      "audioPublicPath": "narration/audio/s002-c005.mp3",
      "audioDurationMs": 500,
      "silentMs": 0,
      "transitionMs": 300,
      "leadInMs": 100,
      "tailMs": 150,
      "transitionFrames": 9,
      "leadInFrames": 3,
      "audioFrames": 15,
      "tailFrames": 5,
      "startFrame": 288,
      "durationInFrames": 32,
      "stateImagePublicPath": "narration/generated/states/s002-c005.png"
    },
    {
      "id": "jsonrpc-plain-object",
      "index": 10,
      "page": 2,
      "click": 6,
      "text": "More importantly, TypeScript only sees a plain object, not an API contract that can evolve together with the server.",
      "audioPublicPath": "narration/audio/s002-c006.mp3",
      "audioDurationMs": 500,
      "silentMs": 0,
      "transitionMs": 300,
      "leadInMs": 100,
      "tailMs": 150,
